\par\par \b \uc2 China Uneasy Leaving Yuan to 'Market Forces' -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2013\par 21:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 15:22 EDT - \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  has been purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "at a frantic rate in recent weeks," says Capital Economics. Firm estimates the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  purchased roughly $70B last month, and notes that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  was stepping in to keep the yuan weak in 3Q when other emerging-market central banks were working to shore up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . CapEcon says the \uc2 PBOC\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been aimed at limiting yuan gains against other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August and September. But ultimately, "China's policymakers remain deeply uncomfortable with allowing market forces a say in determining the exchange rate at times of uncertainty," CapEcon adds. (erin.mccarthy@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:36 EDT - USD/PEN has a natural ceiling of around PEN2.80 to PEN2.83 per US dollar, and if that is tested, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in sol weakness. Firm sees the sol strengthening to PEN2.75 a dollar, from its current 2.77 level. Upbeat data out of China and new investment projects in Peru should support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it adds, though too much strength could also stir up \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a relatively narrow range, preventing too much PEN strength to maintain export competitiveness, and restrict excessive PEN weakness to protect businesses with (unhedged) USD-denominated liabilities," \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says. (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1529 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Erste Bank expects significant HUF weakening versus USD in the medium term. It recommends opening a position in USD/HUF now to play HUF weakening from present local bottom area around 217 towards 230.(veronika.gulyas@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 11:28 EDT - We're going on two weeks without CFTC flow data because of the government shutdown, but if \uc2 UBS\uc2  client data is any indication, there may not be much position shifting in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to report anyway. The investment bank reports \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows stalling last week, with dollar volumes "collapsing" to 77% of its average and euro and sterling activity even weaker. "Not putting trades on appeared to be the preferred expression of risk aversion," \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. Those who were around were mainly real-money asset managers, mostly selling the dollar against euro and yen. (cynthia.lin@wsj.com; @cynthialin_dj)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2181 or john.shipman@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 0000 GMT (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ) \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  is bearish on HUF versus EUR as discussions in the government on a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt relief plan and pre-election news could lead to more short-term weakness and volatility.\par \par \uc2 EUR/HUF is relatively low at 294.81 vs 295.12 late Friday, as a more cautious tone from the the country's rate setters, still-positive real interest rates, a current account surplus, and a more dovish U.S. Fed have recently helped anchor the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Goldman Sach says.\par \par \uc2 However, the structural drivers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain unchanged, and HUF will likely continue to suffer from foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deleveraging and lower potential economic growth in the longer term. The rate differential has narrowed further on the back of more cuts this year and higher U.S. rates, which could also start to erode demand for Hungarian assets. So far, HUF strength has been boosted by the high carry, but the key policy rate has dropped to 3.60% after a series of gradual cuts enacted over the last year or so.\par \par \uc2 Goldman notes however that HUF weakness appears to be one of the policy objectives for the future - but the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aren't willing to allow HUF to depreciate just yet. They first need to reduce foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sensitivity, and are also constrained by the upcoming general elections in spring 2014.\par \par \uc2 (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0000 GMT (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--\par \par \uc2 Tuesday, October 15\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT Spain: EUR3.5B-EUR4.5B 6-month, 12-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT Greece: EUR1.25B 13-week T-bills\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT Switzerland: 91-day T-bills (open volume)\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Hungary: HUF40B 3-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Belgium: EUR1.8B-EUR2.2B 3-month, 12-month Treasury certificates\par \par \uc2 Wednesday, October 16\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Germany: EUR5B 0.25% September 2015 Schatz\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Portugal EUR1.25B-EUR1.5B 3-month, 9-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT Netherlands: target volume for Treasury certificate auction on Oct. 24\par \par \uc2 Thursday, October 17\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT Spain: EUR1.5B-EUR2.5B 3.30% July 2016, 3.75% October 2018\par \par \uc2 0850 GMT France: EUR6B-EUR7B 2.25% February 2016 BTAN, 1.00% November 2018 OAT\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Hungary: HUF18B 5.50% December 2016, HUF15B 5.50% December 2018, HUF10B 6.00% November 2023\par \par \uc2 0950 GMT France: EUR1B-EUR1.5B 2.10% July 2023 OATi, 1.85% July 2027 OATei, 1.80% July 2040 OATei\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT UK: GBP4.75B 1.25% Gilt 2018 (London)\par \par \uc2 1200 GMT Hungary: target volume for 3-month T-bill auction on Oct. 22\par \par \uc2 Friday, October 18\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT France: details of T-bill auction on Oct. 21\par \par \uc2 1300 GMT Poland: details of bond auction on Oct. 22\par \par \uc2 Xxxx Weekly EMU bond supply preview\par \par \uc2 (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1453 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Near-term resistance in USD/JPY at 98.70 is likely to continue capping the topside, says \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , as it has done throughout October. In addition, the 200-day moving average at 96.95 contains any downside probes. When a range break is seen it will likely be to the topside, says \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , targeting first 99.70, and then the September high of 100.60. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:47 EDT - Inflation in India is once again mounting, with consumer and wholesale price indexes rising above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort level. Reduction in fuel subsidies and higher food prices contributed to the spike. Now, India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces a tough balancing act as it tries to stimulate falling growth while keeping prices in check. The rupee's stability in recent weeks gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to unwind some of the tightening measures it introduced this summer to curb the rupee's depreciation. But the country's trade imbalances and weak economic outlook will threaten to weaken the rupee in the coming months, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  analysts say. The dollar up 0.7% to INR61.45. (prabha.natarajan@wsj.com; @prabhanatarajan)\par \par \uc2 1421 GMT xxxx GMT DJ The Polish government bond market has seen interest today from foreign players, who are buying in the belief that significant demand will emerge for papers in coming weeks as players reinvest cash they will receive from the finance ministry in coupons and redemptions. "There is about PLN 30 billion to be redeemed this month, and if even only one third of that is to return to the market it would be a lot," the dealer says. Average yield on Polish two-year bonds is down to 3.07% from 3.13% late Friday, five-year is down to 3.66% from 3.74% and the ten-year paper yields 4.37% today, from 4.42%. (patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1415 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] While Standard Bank's analyst Steven Barrow does not recommend any fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades due to the current tough market conditions ahead of the U.S. debt ceiling deadline, he does point out a change in tack for the Kiwi dollar. Barrow says the bank's indicators have turned neutral on EUR/NZD, where they have been short from 1.6370 on October 7. Current rate is 1.6220. For AUD/NZD, the indicator has turned long, from a neutral stance taken on September 24 when the cross was trading at 1.1330, pretty much where it is right now. -- (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1411 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The decision of \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave rates unchanged was priced in and has not moved ruble or bond prices, although the tone of its statement turned more dovish, Capital Economics says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted a drop in inflation and omitted last month's line that rates were at an appropriate level to balance inflation and growth risks. Thus, "with inflation now falling, there may be room for modest rate cuts in the next six months," Capital Economics says. It expects the first move to ease policy to happen by the end of this year, and sees a cumulative 75 bps cut over the next half of the year. (andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 09:51 EDT - Instead of the 4.7% annualized growth expected of Peru in August, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says the economy likely expanded by 4.5%. Firm points to still-depressed business confidence and a deceleration in construction, even though domestic consumption has held up. Another reason for the pullback is mathematic: there are fewer working days this August than in August 2012. The Peru government will release its August growth indicator on Tuesday. (robert.kozak@wsj.com) [ 14-10-13 1922GMT ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020131014e9ae000k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
