\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen Continuing With  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Defend Sol\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 17:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 --With the sol coming under heavy depreciation pressures, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  is expected to continue to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 Banks, private pension funds and foreign investors, among others, have dumped soles in recent weeks, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase efforts to ensure the sol doesn't weaken too much, which would run the risk of importing inflation and hurting borrowers who earn in soles but have debts in dollars.\par \par \uc2 So far this week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $950 million in spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has also placed dollar-indexed certificates of deposit, which help ease dollar gains.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a report Friday that despite an acceleration in inflation in Peru, its weakening economy is expected to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrain from increasing interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Meanwhile, we expect it (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to use strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $4.2 billion since May. That is a sharp turnaround from the previous three years, in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net total of $25.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 Last year the sol appreciated more than 5.0% against the greenback, despite purchases of $13.2 billion by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012.\par \par \uc2 But fears that the U.S. Federal Reserve could take the foot off the gas of its monetary easing, a decline in capital inflows, and poorer mineral prices that have cut into Peru's exports, are among the factors that have led to weaker demand for the sol.\par \par \uc2 So far this year through Thursday the sol has depreciated 10.19%.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been increasing the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate market to keep the sol limited, under pressure from a sizable current account deficit and the need to protect the financial sector from a rapid depreciation as well as to limit pass-through effects on inflation," BofA \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has no fixed rate for sol against the greenback, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lessen volatility.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 23, 2013 11:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130823e98n004ab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
