\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT: Mexican energy overhaul disappoints peso\b0\par\par\uc2 1,404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2013\par 19:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Mexican peso weakens against the U.S. dollar, to MXN12.6455 vs MXN12.5670 in morning trade, after President \uc2 Enrique Pena Nieto\uc2  outlined his proposed energy reform. The President emphasized that Mexico would retain ownership of its oil wealth under his plan, suggesting profit-sharing contracts with drillers but not production-sharing contracts. Markets were expecting something more aggressive, said Antonio Magana, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Mexican brokerage Interacciones. Yet the sell-off could be an over-reaction. "This still isn't the definitive" reform, he warned. (amy.guthrie@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Mexican peso weakens against the U.S. dollar, to MXN12.6455 vs MXN12.5670 in morning trade, after President \uc2 Enrique Pena Nieto\uc2  outlined his proposed energy reform. The President emphasized that Mexico would retain ownership of its oil wealth under his plan, suggesting profit-sharing contracts with drillers but not production-sharing contracts. Markets were expecting something more aggressive, said Antonio Magana, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Mexican brokerage Interacciones. Yet the sell-off could be an over-reaction. "This still isn't the definitive" reform, he warned. (amy.guthrie@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  say they "still believe Peru's government is determined in drawing a line at 2.80" for the Peruvian sol against the US dollar because policymakers don't feel comfortable with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker than that. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market amid PEN weakness. "We expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue as needed given the high dollarization of the economy: 48% of credit to the private sector is in dollars," BofA adds. And with inflation rising above its upper target range in July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not tolerate much more PEN weakness. USD/PEN last up 0.1% at 2.796. (erin.mccarthy@wsj.com; @eemccarthy)\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  say they "still believe Peru's government is determined in drawing a line at 2.80" for the Peruvian sol against the US dollar because policymakers don't feel comfortable with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker than that. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market amid PEN weakness. "We expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue as needed given the high dollarization of the economy: 48% of credit to the private sector is in dollars," BofA adds. And with inflation rising above its upper target range in July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not tolerate much more PEN weakness. USD/PEN last up 0.1% at 2.796. (erin.mccarthy@wsj.com; @eemccarthy)\par \par \uc2 Trading in emerging-market credit default swaps rose to $279B in 2Q, according to a survey of 13 major dealers taken by trade group EMTA. That volume is a 28% increase over the previous year and 31% increase over the previous quarter. Broad concerns about the health of emerging markets has increased CDS demand from hedgers and speculators, said Jane Brauer of \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 , though the increase in CDS trading was uneven across the globe. The EU's ban on speculative trades lowered the volumes from that region, while Asia and Latin America showed increases. Brazil represented the largest CDS volume last quarter at $65B. (prabha.natarajan@wsj.com; @prabhanatarajan)\par \par \uc2 Trading in emerging-market credit default swaps rose to $279B in 2Q, according to a survey of 13 major dealers taken by trade group EMTA. That volume is a 28% increase over the previous year and 31% increase over the previous quarter. Broad concerns about the health of emerging markets has increased CDS demand from hedgers and speculators, said Jane Brauer of \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 , though the increase in CDS trading was uneven across the globe. The EU's ban on speculative trades lowered the volumes from that region, while Asia and Latin America showed increases. Brazil represented the largest CDS volume last quarter at $65B. (prabha.natarajan@wsj.com; @prabhanatarajan)\par \par \uc2 Angel Garcia Banchs, the head of Venezuelan business consultancy Econometrica, believes that the country's system of dollar auctions, launched to pump hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the economy, will be a failed stopgap. Many had hoped the auction system would allow Venezuela's private sector to influence the exchange rate at which the auctioned dollars are awarded. Garcia says that with three auctions completed, it is clear that it's still "the state, arbitrarily, setting the rate." Many analysts have also noted that the auctions have provided fewer dollars than the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism it replaced earlier this year. (ezequiel.minaya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Angel Garcia Banchs, the head of Venezuelan business consultancy Econometrica, believes that the country's system of dollar auctions, launched to pump hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the economy, will be a failed stopgap. Many had hoped the auction system would allow Venezuela's private sector to influence the exchange rate at which the auctioned dollars are awarded. Garcia says that with three auctions completed, it is clear that it's still "the state, arbitrarily, setting the rate." Many analysts have also noted that the auctions have provided fewer dollars than the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism it replaced earlier this year. (ezequiel.minaya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 David Rosenberg\uc2 , chief economist and strategist at Gluskin/Sheff, says there's a dearth of evidence to build a case for a collapse in Canada's housing market: existing home sales are running at double-digit rates year-over-year; average home prices ran up 5% from a year ago in June; and, despite the unexpected falloff in building permits in June, total ground-breakings in July totaled 193K annualized units, almost unchanged from June. "All in, it looks increasingly convincing to us that the there is no hard landing but stabilization in the Canadian housing market after the government ushered in more restrictive mortgage insurance rules aimed at curbing runaway household debt levels and cooling down the red-hot residential segment last year," he says. (don.curren@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 David Rosenberg\uc2 , chief economist and strategist at Gluskin/Sheff, says there's a dearth of evidence to build a case for a collapse in Canada's housing market: existing home sales are running at double-digit rates year-over-year; average home prices ran up 5% from a year ago in June; and, despite the unexpected falloff in building permits in June, total ground-breakings in July totaled 193K annualized units, almost unchanged from June. "All in, it looks increasingly convincing to us that the there is no hard landing but stabilization in the Canadian housing market after the government ushered in more restrictive mortgage insurance rules aimed at curbing runaway household debt levels and cooling down the red-hot residential segment last year," he says. (don.curren@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Of all data releases, surprises in monthly nonfarm payrolls move bonds and stocks most. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  finds that a 1-standard-deviation surprise--about a 80K swing--causes an average 5-basis-point move in the 10-year yield and 0.3% impact on the S&P 500. But when it comes to predictive powers for how the economy will actually fare in the months ahead, the investment bank finds payrolls has little. Instead, the Philly Fed and ISM manufacturing reports best illustrate the economy's strength and momentum. Those reports are both more timely (released shortly after surveys are taken) and subject to smaller revisions, says Goldman. The latest data from both were also surprisingly upbeat, contrasting the underwhelming July jobs. August Philly Fed comes Thursday. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com; cynthialin_dj)\par \par \uc2 Of all data releases, surprises in monthly nonfarm payrolls move bonds and stocks most. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  finds that a 1-standard-deviation surprise--about a 80K swing--causes an average 5-basis-point move in the 10-year yield and 0.3% impact on the S&P 500. But when it comes to predictive powers for how the economy will actually fare in the months ahead, the investment bank finds payrolls has little. Instead, the Philly Fed and ISM manufacturing reports best illustrate the economy's strength and momentum. Those reports are both more timely (released shortly after surveys are taken) and subject to smaller revisions, says Goldman. The latest data from both were also surprisingly upbeat, contrasting the underwhelming July jobs. August Philly Fed comes Thursday. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com; cynthialin_dj) [ 12-08-13 1754GMT ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130812e98c000o4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
