\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru's Sol Seen Gaining After Hiccup That Weakened  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2013\par 18:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Sol seen appreciating after period of weakness\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong economic fundamentals seen helping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen easing volatility\par \par \uc2 By Robert Kozak\par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 --After weakening recently, Peru's sol appears set to regain its appreciation trend, as strong economic fundamentals again propel the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sol gained 5.4% against the U.S. dollar last year on strong capital inflows, despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars.\par \par \uc2 Short-term factors weakened the sol in April and May, such as greater demand for greenbacks by companies to pay dividends outside of Peru. Political noise, tied in good part to the chance of greater government activity in the petroleum sector, also weakened the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals are there for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to strengthen, but probably not at a pace in which it was happening in the past," Credicorp General Manager Walter Bayly said Tuesday in a conference call with analysts. Credicorp is the nation's largest financial-services company.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the sol closed slightly stronger at PEN2.614 per dollar, bringing the depreciation of the sol so far this year to 2.43%.\par \par \uc2 Scotiabank in Peru forecasts the sol will make up lost ground in coming days, "and continue appreciating at a moderate rhythm." That appreciation will be limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, it added.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or BCRP, has shown its willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, although it has been absent since April 19.\par \par \uc2 "We turn constructive on the sol given the political uncertainty, which had weighed on the sol the last two weeks, appears to be easing, and the risk of higher commodity price volatility should be limited by BCRP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $13.2 billion in spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, and so far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $5.21 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken other measures, such as regularly increasing the amount that private pension funds can invest abroad. It has also increased commercial bank reserve requirements for U.S. dollars a number of times in order to choke off credit growth, and ease appreciation pressures.\par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said Tuesday that some of the additional reserves bought by the BCRP are being sold to the treasury for the prepayment of debt with multilaterals and deposits in the stabilization fund.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says that with the treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost complete, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could decline in coming months, leaving space for some appreciation of the sol, although that could be limited due to other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the exchange rate to fluctuate around USD/PEN 2.60-2.55 range the rest of the year, breaking the appreciation trend of recent years," it said.\par \par \uc2 -Ryan Dube contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 07, 2013 12:03 ET (16:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130507e957004ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
