\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Pauses Dollar Buying  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 16:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken a pause in its daily purchases of U.S. dollars, without formally announcing any change to its policy.\par \par \uc2 In late August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to purchase greenbacks every day, in part aiming to introduce uncertainty in what had become a one-way bet on sol appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has refrained from purchasing dollars on three separate trading sessions this year, but the latest pause has been the longest since it bought into effect its daily purchases.\par \par \uc2 Since purchasing $10 million on Feb. 25, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't bought any dollars.\par \par \uc2 "They haven't announced it, but the facts reflect the fact that the policy of dollar buying remains discretional," Scotiabank economist Mario Guerrero said Monday.\par \par \uc2 So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $3.36 billion, following a record-buying spree of $13.2 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said there hasn't been any change in the bank's policy regarding buying dollars.\par \par \uc2 Strong inflows of capital into Peru last year helped the sol appreciate 5.4% against the dollar, despite the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has initiated a number of measures aimed at curbing the strength of the sol, including increasing commercial bank reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 The strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised the ire of exporters.\par \par \uc2 Following the introduction of various government measures the sol has depreciated 1.68% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak.dube@dowjones.com [ 04-03-13 1548GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130304e934000om\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
