\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Finish Lower; Sol Weaker Versus Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Dube   \par \uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2013\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock-market indexes closed lower Thursday, following a decline in metal prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index ended 0.14% lower at 20611.68.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index fell 0.58% to close at 31238.32.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) decreased 3.68% to end at $34.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) finished 1.54% weaker at $25.60.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was \uc2 Intercorp Financial Services Inc\uc2 . (IFS.VL), which gained 1.39% to close at $40. Intercorp owns Peru's fourth-biggest bank, an insurance company and a supermarket chain.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, the third consecutive session that it hasn't bought dollars on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in part to make the appreciation trend of the sol less pronounced. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't defend any fixed exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed weaker Thursday at PEN2.59 per dollar, compared with PEN2.582 in the previous session. The sol appreciated 5.4% against the U.S. dollar in 2012, but so far this year it has weakened 1.49%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com [ 02-28-13 1640ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130228e92s0