\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Sharply Higher; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2013\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock-market indexes ended sharply higher Friday, on gains in various blue-chip shares.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index rose 1.70% to end at 21800.27 and the blue-chip Selective Index ended 1.55% higher at 32721.12.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) rose 0.79% at end at $38.30 as copper prices improved. Financial-holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP), which owns \uc2 Banco de Credito\uc2 , Peru's largest bank, rose 1.74% to end at $158.60.\par \par \uc2 Base-metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 1.09% to end at $39.70, on gains in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the company said its fourth-quarter net income totaled $531.8 million, compared with $537 million in the same period a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy $160 million at an average price of PEN2.5698 for each U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in part to make the appreciation trend of the sol less pronounced. It doesn't defend any fixed-exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed weaker against the dollar at PEN2.578, compared with PEN2.576 in the previous trading session.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com [ 02-01-13 1634ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020130201e92100068\par 