\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  to Buy Dollars for First Time Since August\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Dube   \par \uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2013\par 20:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  held off Thursday from purchasing U.S. dollars in the spot market for the first time in more than five months, as the sol depreciated almost 1% against the greenback in January.\par \par \uc2 In September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its policy for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying a fixed amount of dollars each day, regardless of whether the sol was appreciating or depreciating against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The change was aimed at curbing the appeal of dollar-denominated loans by creating more uncertainty for individuals who believed the sol would continue appreciating.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $13.2 billion in spot-market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, however the sol still appreciated 5.4% against the dollar in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't buy dollars was on Aug. 24.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had maintained its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach so far this year, even though the sol had been depreciating against the dollar in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $1.8 billion so far this year in daily purchases that ranged between $10 million to $350 million.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't immediately available to comment if the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was changing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the sol closed at 2.576 soles per dollar, compared with PEN2.568 in the previous session. The sol depreciated 0.94% against the greenback in January.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com [ 01-31-13 1441ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130131e91v000ng\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
