\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2013\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Thursday, as a number of mining companies gained ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index rose 0.61% to end at 21,435.29. The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.60% higher at 32,222.11.\par \par \uc2 Base and precious metals mining company \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) gained 0.76% to end at 2.66 soles ($1.03), while tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) rose 1.31% to end at PEN2.32.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 0.18% to end at $39.27, on an improvement in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in five months.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  every day in part to make the appreciation trend of the sol less pronounced. It doesn't defend any fixed exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed weaker at PEN2.576 to the dollar, compared with PEN2.568 to the dollar in the previous trading session.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com [ 01-31-13 1632ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020130131e91v0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
