\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Strengthening Sol Sparks Debate Between Government, Business\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2013\par 21:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Strength of Peruvian sol pits business sector against government\par \par \uc2 --Exporter group wants more government measures\par \par \uc2 --Exporters say strong sol is cutting into profit margins\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Robert Kozak \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA, Peru--The strength of Peru's sol has sparked a heated debate between the government and business sector about what should be done, with exporters leading protests after the sol gained 5.3% against the U.S. dollar last year on strong capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made further gains early this year, and former prime minister Pedro Pablo Kuczynski, an investment banker, recently forecast that the sol could reach PEN2.30 to the U.S. dollar this year from around MXN2.55 at present, damaging the business sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government has taken a number of indirect measures, such as increasing reserve requirements, most recently at the start of this year, in order to weaken credit growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Central Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strongly, buying $1.5 billion so far this year and helping to turn back some of the sol's gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In all of 2012, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought $13.2 billion in the exchange market, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's chief economist said recently there is no limit on how many dollars the bank can purchase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Friday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased to 32% from 30% the maximum amount of assets under management that private pension funds can invest outside of Peru in what \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  called "an attempt to counter large \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows into the country."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The business sector wants more, however, pointing out that the strong sol means imports are growing much faster than exports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The main private-sector association of Peruvian exporters, known as ADEX, wants the finance ministry to prepay external debt, something the finance minister has said could take place this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ADEX's chief economist, Carlos Gonzalez, told Dow Jones Newswires Monday that profits for companies that export manufactured products fall sharply as the sol appreciates. The association says lower profits damp corporate investments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The exporters want a series of new measures, including a government crackdown on illegal activities, such as illegal gold mining and narcotics trafficking, which create greater inflows of cash and demand for the sol. Money laundering in Peru is estimated to be worth from $6.5 billion to $7.0 billion a year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government has responded by pointing to strong export growth in recent years, adding that exporters must become more efficient.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Luis Miguel Castilla said that in the last decade the sol has appreciated by about 30%, while nontraditional exports, such as manufactured products, have increased fivefold, government agency Andina reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to Andina, Mr. Castilla said that if inflationary pressures trend lower then it might be a good idea to eventually debate whether there should be a decline in the reference interest rate, which has been at 4.25% since May 2011. That would help weaken capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com [ 01-21-13 1512ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130121e91l0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
