\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  sol up nearly 6 pct in 2012 despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2012\par 20:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (New throughout, adds comparison with forecasts, background, details)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, Dec 28 (Reuters) - Peru's sol closed at 2.552 per U.S. dollar on Friday, ending the year with gains of 5.72 percent despite record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which purchased $13.85 billion in U.S. dollars to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advances to a 16-year high.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters at the start of the year predicted the sol would remain nearly unchanged at around 2.68, while a few predicted a gain of as much as 3 percent to 2.60.\par \par \uc2 Peru's strong economy and the U.S. Federal Reserve's stimulus helped stoke the sol's advances, leaving \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trying to soak up excess liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the local spot market every day since Aug. 27 but only managed to slow the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation, not stop it.\par \par \uc2 This year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also restricted the ability of banks to make bets in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and tightened reserve requirements several times to stem the inflow of speculative capital as the sol reached levels not seen since 1996.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended bidding at 2.546 per dollar on Thursday - its strongest level in more than 16 years - but finished the year slightly weaker after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $40 million on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters analysis after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  announced its third round of financial easing in September said the sol would finish bidding this year at 2.55 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, performance in the stock market turned out to be less robust than analysts predicted.\par \par \uc2 At the start of 2012, equity analysts surveyed by Reuters said Lima's main stock index would finish the year with gains of between 15 percent and 30 percent.\par \par \uc2 Though the index did rise 23.5 percent through April, it then retreated on a host of worries - from the slowdown in China, to debt woes in Europe, to a sluggish U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 As of Friday, Lima's bourse was on track to finish the year at around 20,400 points, a rise of just 4 percent. It will be open for limited trade on Monday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Ursula Scollo; Editing by David Gregorio)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU/SOL (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121228e8cs000qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
