\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-South America sees new  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  wars despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cost\b0\par\par\uc2 1,020 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2012\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost over $13 billion in last 2-1/2 years\par \par \uc2 * High opportunity cost for $135 billion dollar purchases\par \par \uc2 * Policymakers fret about new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure\par \par \uc2 By Krista Hughes\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Dec 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cost South America's central banks more than $13 billion in the last 2-1/2 years but they are likely to maintain their defenses against hot money inflows if a fresh rush of cheap money sparks another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars.\par \par \uc2 Latin American finance ministers meeting in Chile on Friday said monetary easing in developed countries could hurt their export competitiveness by pushing up \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region - a problem they have been wrestling with since the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Bank of England Governor \uc2 Mervyn King\uc2  warned last week that a 2013 might see a growing number of countries deliberately weakening their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offset the impact of a slow global economy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows Brazil, Chile, Colombia and Peru have bought $135 billion in dollars to help keep a lid on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-2010, just before the U.S. Federal Reserve announced its last round of monetary easing, dubbed QE2.\par \par \uc2 The Fed is now well into QE3, and Chilean Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said Wednesday's decision to further bolster U.S. asset purchases was a "source of worry" for all emerging markets with healthy growth and floating exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Low interest rates in advanced economies encourage investors to seek higher returns in faster-growing emerging markets such as Latin America, but accelerating capital inflows put unwelcome upward pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making exports more expensive.\par \par \uc2 "This is the third round of QE and we are starting at a level where the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are a lot stronger," said Jefferies Latin America strategist Siobhan Morden, who sees \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the biggest concern for investors in local debt.\par \par \uc2 "It clearly places more stress on policymakers in how to manage this liquidity."\par \par \uc2 Low inflation in Peru, Chile and Colombia and healthy budget balances give central banks plenty of leeway to keep buying dollars, adding to already-swollen reserves, analysts said - a contrast to the last round of QE, when many countries were struggling with inflation fanned by a V-shaped recovery.\par \par \uc2 Most dollar purchases so far have been offset by market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as issuing bonds, to mop up or sterilize excess liquidity - but these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a high cost due to the gap between very low U.S. yields and higher local interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Calculations by Thomson Reuters put the accumulated opportunity cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases from mid-2010 to November 2012 at about $13.9 billion, more than $11 billion in Brazil alone, without taking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations into account.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's cost reflects benchmark interest rates which were as high as 12.5 percent in mid-2011, before an aggressive easing cycle which slashed them to a record low 7.25 percent, while U.S. official rates were - and are - close to zero.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cost Chile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Colombia between $500 million and $1 billion each, according to estimates based on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data on reserve asset returns, or local and U.S. market interest rates where not.\par \par \uc2 DIFFERENT STROKES\par \par \uc2 Officials attending the Community of Latin American and Caribbean States (CELAC) meeting in Chile did not come up with a joint solution on how best to handle hot money flows, but agreed they were a major challenge to the region.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has slapped strict controls on foreign investment and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in markets, while the Andean nations have largely eschewed capital controls and analysts expect they will continue to rely on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future.\par \par \uc2 While Brazil and Chile have scaled back or paused their \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Colombia remain very active in the market - despite having an even higher interest rate gap with the United States than they did in mid-2010.\par \par \uc2 Colombia has picked up the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying 18.5 percent more dollars in the 11 months to November than in all of 2011, and traders are also wary of Chile, where the peso has appreciated 9.5 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Peru has bought a record $13 billion so far in 2012 and has also limited banks' ability to make big bets in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with tighter rules on forwards.\par \par \uc2 Subdued inflation in Peru, Colombia and Chile means those central banks have less reason to worry about the impact of liquidity created by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which depends on demand for local paper to mop up the extra funds.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it has the scope to do so," said Nomura Securities economist Benito Berber.\par \par \uc2 Compared to August 2010, just before the Fed flagged its QE2 easing, the Peruvian sol is up 9 percent, the Chilean peso up 5 percent and the Colombian peso up 1 percent, although Brazil's real is weaker thanks to concerted official efforts.\par \par \uc2 Brazil confused many by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December after a sharp weakening when third quarter growth came in well below expectations.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers have indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize somewhere between 2.0 and 2.1 per dollar, and it is unlikely to tolerate a sharp strengthening.\par \par \uc2 Economist Intelligence Unit analyst Anna Szterenfeld said Brazil was likely to face less upward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure given recent rate cuts there, compared with rate increases during the Fed's QE2 period. "Some yield-seeking investors - Brazil would call them speculators - won't find Brazil as attractive as they did then," she said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo, Anthony Esposito and Alexandra Ulmer in Santiago, Nelson Bocanegra and Jack Kimball in Bogota, Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City, Terry Wade and Mitra Taj in Lima and Jeoff Hall from IFR; editing by Kieran Murray and Todd Eastham)\par \par \uc2 LATINAMERICA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNA | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121217e8ch000hh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
