\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sees More Room for  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -Report\b0\par\par\uc2 127 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2012\par 17:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:21 EST - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Director General Renzo Rossini says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to buy US dollars next year at the same pace it did this year. So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought almost $13 billion, far above 2011's $3.5 billion. Rossini told newspaper Gestion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to sterilize dollar purchases, and that, "there is a lot of space" to continue buying. Rossini said that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls were always a possibility in extreme cases but ruled them out for now saying that inflows of capital into Peru are long-term, not hot money. (robert.kozak@dowjones.com) [ 17-12-12 1621GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121217e8ch000pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
