\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2012\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Monday, as some blue-chip shares gained ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index rose 0.1% to end at 21,060.33.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.4% higher at 31,471.40.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) rose 1.1% to end at $137. It owns Peru's biggest bank, \uc2 Banco de Credito\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Peruvian cement producer Cementos Pacasmayo SAA (CPAC, CPACASC1.VL) gained 1.3% to end at 6.28 soles. ($2.40).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to buy $10 million at an average of 2.6142 Peruvian soles per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase U.S. dollars on a regular basis, in part to reverse an ongoing appreciation trend in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed unchanged Monday at PEN2.613 per dollar. So far this year, the sol has strengthened 3.1% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 A poll carried out by the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  shows the sol is expected to steadily appreciate over the next two years.\par \par \uc2 The 21 economic analysts surveyed said the sol will end this year at PEN2.58 per dollar, at PEN2.53 per dollar in 2013 and at PEN2.50 per dollar in 2014.\par \par \uc2 The sol has been appreciating in part due to Peru's strong economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at