\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Finish Higher; Sol Slightly Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Dube   \par \uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2012\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher on Thursday, as shares of some blue-chip companies posted strong gains.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index rose 1.09% to close at 21114.95.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index gained 1.72% to end at 31449.46.\par \par \uc2 Financial-holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL) finished 1.76% higher at $133, following the release of strong third-quarter results. Credicorp, which owns Peru's largest bank, \uc2 Banco de Credito\uc2 , reported late Wednesday that its net income increased 33% in the third quarter to $227.5 million.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals mining company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) increased 1.56% to close at $35.70.\par \par \uc2 Silver and lead mining company \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) ended 3.19% higher at 2.59 soles ($0.99).\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to buy $20 million at an average of PEN2.6079 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase U.S. dollars on a regular basis, in part to reverse an ongoing appreciation trend in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sol closed slightly weaker Thursday at PEN2.609 per dollar, compared to PEN2.608 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has strengthened 3.26% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 BBVA\uc2  Banco Continental, the second biggest bank in Peru, said Thursday that it expects the sol to continue its appreciating trend and end 2013 around PEN2.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Even though we don't rule out episodes of turbulence, we expect that the appreciating trend will continue in the following months," the bank said. "There is a large appetite for domestic assets and the capital inflows have strengthened the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 -Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com [ 11-08-12 1629ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020121108e8b80004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
