\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol to Continue With Appreciating Trend -Pension Funds\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak  \par \uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2012\par 21:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's private sector pension funds, which manage some of the largest investment funds in the nation, expect the sol to continue appreciating against the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The sol has gained 4.38% against the greenback so far this year, and 5.29% over the last 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 "It is a question of the velocity rather than the direction," Renzo Castellano, director of investments for \uc2 AFP Horizonte\uc2 , said in a meeting with reporters Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Vicente Tuesta, director of investments for AFP Profuturo, said at the same meeting that strong economic fundamentals have helped the sol appreciate, and that this appreciation isn't expected to ease in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 Peru's gross domestic product expanded by 6.1% in the first half of the year. The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  forecasts growth of 6% in GDP for the full year.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  President Julio Velarde told a commission of Congress that the appreciation of the sol has been close to the average of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region that have gained, although with less volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to ease volatility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In the three trading sessions this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased a total of $380 million. So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased about $11 billion.\par \par \uc2 The private pension funds, known as AFPs, have posted returns of more than 9% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 There are four AFPs in Peru. \uc2 AFP Horizonte SA\uc2  (HORIZC1.VL) is owned mainly by Holding Continental and Spain's \uc2 Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria SA\uc2  (\uc2 BBVA\uc2 , BBVA.MC). \uc2 AFP Integra SA\uc2  (INTEGRC1.VL) is owned by Colombia's \uc2 Grupo de Inversiones Suramericana SA\uc2  (GIVSY, GRUPOSURA.BO). AFP Profuturo's main shareholder is a unit of \uc2 Bank of Nova Scotia\uc2  (BNS, BNS.T), while Prima AFP is controlled by Peru's \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL).\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com [ 10-17-12 1530ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121017e8ah000o8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
