\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up on US data, Peru sol at 16-year high\b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2012\par 23:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Refiles to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2  * US retail sales come in stronger than expected\par \par \uc2  * Peru buys $130 mln in biggest daily move since August\par \par \uc2  * Mexican peso firms 0.43 pct, Brazil real up 0.32 pct \par \par \uc2  By Jean Arce and Ursula Scollo\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY/LIMA, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Monday after U.S. retail sales data eased concerns about the outlook of the world's top economy, driving Peru's sol to a nearly 16-year high despite market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Data showed U.S. retail sales in rose a higher-than-expected 1.1 percent last month, improving economic prospects for the United States, the main destination of Mexican exports.\par \par \uc2  "You can start to see the recovery in the United States and that is what is encouraging markets a bit," said Jose Curiel, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Intercam brokerage in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso  gained 0.43 percent to 12.8075 per U.S. dollar while in Brazil, the real   bid 0.32 percent stronger at 2.0340 per greenback at the local close.\par \par \uc2  Analysts said the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could remain stuck in recent trading ranges as the markets await a solution to Europe's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2  Investors are watching closely for signs that Spain is ready to formally request financial aid, a step seen as crucial to curb the spread of the euro zone crisis.\par \par \uc2  Madrid could finally ask for financial aid from the euro zone next month, officials said. \par \par \uc2  "We have this situation with the United States growing, but slowly. And Europe continues with its problems," said Ures Folchini, a treasury vice president at \uc2 WestLB\uc2  bank in Sao Paulo. "It's not an optimistic scenario, it's a scenario where you want to protect your capital and wait."\par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of economists showed on Monday that Brazil will likely hold its benchmark interest rate at its current level of 7.25 percent through the end of this year, ending a year-long cycle of rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Latin America's biggest economy cut its key interest rate to 7.25 percent, an all-time low.\par \par \uc2  Monetary stimulus programs in the United States and Europe are expected to keep driving investors toward higher-yielding emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2  Brazil, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Colombia have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to fight the appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect local manufacturers from cheaper imports.\par \par \uc2  Markets in Colombia and Chile were closed for the Columbus Day holiday.\par \par \uc2  Peru's sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed to its strongest in nearly 16 years against the dollar even as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $130 million - its biggest daily dollar purchase since the end of August.\par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it routinely does in the market, but its (dollar) purchases lack the force to even cause a hiccup in the exchange rate," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought a record of nearly $11.6 billion so far this year, but the sol has still advanced more than 4 percent against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2100 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                               Daily  Year-to-\par                                         pct   ate pct\par                            Latest    change    change\par Brazil real                  2.0340      0.32     -8.20\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.8050      2.73      9.09\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.1800      0.32    -23.46\par                                              \par Chile peso                 472.2000    Closed      9.97\par                                              \par Colombia peso               1797.65    Closed    7.83\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.5810      0.15      4.49\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par                                                      \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Natalia Cacioli in Sao Paulo, writing\par by Michael O'Boyle; editing by Gary Crosse)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) (REPEAT) | ABN | D | M | RBN | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121018e8af001gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
