\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2012\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's stock-market indexes ended lower Friday, dragged down by weakness in a number of blue-chip shares.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index fell 0.28% to end at 21,674.79. The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.19% lower at 31,842.21.\par \par \uc2 For the third quarter, the General Index rose 7.2%, while the Selective Index gained 7.9%.\par \par \uc2 Companies tied to Peru's robust domestic demand have led the gains in the main stock indexes so far this year. Cement producers have gained on red-hot activity in the construction sector, while food and beverage producers and the financial sector have also been impressive performers.\par \par \uc2 Economists expect Peru's strong economic growth, which has helped boost the stock market, to continue.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said in a report it expects 6.5% growth in Peru's gross domestic product this year.\par \par \uc2 "Growth acceleration continues, driven by a boost to public-sector spending. However, we expect this boost to be largely transitory as the economy converges to sustainable growth next year. In this context inflation should be well behaved," it said.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BUENAVC1.Vl) fell 0.41% to $38.70 as the price of gold eased.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) lost 0.90% to $124.30. It owns Peru's largest bank, \uc2 Banco de Credito\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to buy $40 million at an average of PEN2.5978 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased more than $10 billion so far this year with its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sol closed slightly weaker at PEN2.599 against the dollar compared with PEN2.597 in the previous session. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.63% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@dowjones.com [ 09-28-12 1642ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120928e89s000xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
