\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2012\par 22:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Peru--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Thursday, tracking international markets that gained as concerns about the European debt crisis eased.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index rose 0.7% to end at 21736.07.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index increased 0.83% to finish at 31904.35\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL) gained 1.23% to close at $125.43. Credicorp owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Tin-mining company Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) ended 0.4% higher at 2.49 soles ($0.96).\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) climbed 0.99% to close at $38.86.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to buy $100 million at an average of 2.5946 Peruvian soles per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase U.S. dollars on a regular basis, in part to reverse an ongoing appreciation trend in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought more than $10 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed weaker Thursday at PEN2.597 per dollar compared to PEN2.595 in the previous session. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.71% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com [ 09-27-12 1624ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000